'''Pokémon HeartGold SoulSilver: Pokédex Completion Comic'''<!--(Japanese: ''Pokémon HeartGold SoulSilver: Pokédex Completion Comic'')--> is a one-shot {{pkmn|manga}} created by [[Makoto Mizobuchi]]. It was published in the October 2009 edition of [[CoroCoro|Bessatsu CoroCoro Comic Special]], in a separate volume titled ''Pokémon HeartGold SoulSilver Official Fanbook'' (ポケモン　ハートゴールド・ソウルシルバー　公式ファンブック).

==Plot==
A {{pkmn|Trainer}} named {{OBP|Soul|PCC}} attempts to {{pkmn2|caught|capture}} a {{pkmn2|wild}} {{p|Sentret}}, but due to his lack of knowledge, he fails to capture it and {{ga|Lyra|another Trainer}} shows up to help him. After weakening the Pokémon, Soul manages to catch it and then attempts to catch a wild {{p|Bellsprout}}. Soul's {{p|Cyndaquil}} accidentally defeats the Bellsprout, however, and Soul is unable to capture it. The Trainer helps him again and Soul then manages to catch a wild {{p|Growlithe}}. As Soul is about to leave to a new area to find more Pokémon, the Trainer stops him and teaches him that he can [[Fishing|fish]] for Pokémon in bodies of water, that different Pokémon appear at different [[time]]s of the day, and that some Pokémon can be found by using {{m|Headbutt}} on {{FB|Headbutt|tree}}s.

The two are then interrupted by a wild {{p|Steelix}} and Soul tries to fight it with Cyndaquil. The Steelix tackles Cyndaquil and Soul realizes that the Steelix is too strong. The Trainer hands him a [[Heavy Ball]] and tells him to use it. Soul has Cyndaquil use {{m|Flamethrower}}, and whilst the Steelix is engulfed in the flames, he throws the Heavy Ball and catches it. The Trainer explains that the Heavy Ball was made from [[Apricorn]]s and the [[Poké Ball]] smith [[Kurt]] makes them as well as seven other types with its own feature. Soul shouts that he is aiming towards completing the [[Pokédex]].

